       ppmtospu - convert a PPM image to an Atari Spectrum 512 image


SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ppppmmttoossppuu

       [--dd00|--dd22|--dd44] [_p_p_m_f_i_l_e]

       All  options  can  be abbreviated to their shortest unique prefix.  You
       may use two hyphens instead of one.  You may separate  an  option  name
       and its value with white space instead of an equals sign.


DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       This  program converts from the PPM format to the uncompressed Spectrum
       512 image format used on Atari ST computers.

       Input comes from the file you name with the _p_p_m_f_i_l_e argument, or  Stan‐
       dard Input by default.  Output goes to Standard Output.

       The  input  must be 320 pixels wide by 200 pixels high.  If you have an
       image of a different size, you can use ppaammccuutt or ppaammssccaallee to  force  it
       to these dimensions.



OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In  addition  to  the options common to all programs based on libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ ), ppppmmttoossppuu  recognizes  the
       following command line options:



       --dd00    The program does no dithering.


       --dd22    The program uses a 2x2 ordered dither.

              This is the default.


       --dd44    The program uses a 4x4 ordered dither.





